Write a program that accepts an arithmetic expression or a simple assignment statement (e.g., a = b + c * d).

(a) Performs lexical analysis and parsing (you may use a recursive descent parser or operator-precedence parsing).

(b) Generates Three-Address Code for the given expression.

(c) Optionally converts the Three-Address Code into Quadruple and Triple representations.

(d) Handles basic operators: +, -, *, /, and assignment =.

(e) Use temporary variables (e.g., t1, t2, …) for intermediate results.
